New endpoints (app/api/curriculum.py):
- GET /api/v1/levels — public, active levels only (moved here from main.py).
- POST /api/v1/levels, PATCH /api/v1/levels/{id} — ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN only; duplicate display_order re
- GET /api/v1/levels/{id}/materials — public, shows only is_published materials; staff (INSTRUCTOR/ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN) also see unpublished ones, via a new get_current_user_optional dependency that doesn't hard-fail when there's no
  token.
- POST /api/v1/levels/{id}/materials, PATCH /api/v1/materials/{id}, DELETE /api/v1/materials/{id} — INSTRUCTOR/ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN only.

Bug caught and fixed during testing: :content::jsonb in raw SQL silently broke — SQLAlchemy's text() treats :: as an escaped literal colon (it's how you'd write a literal : in a query string), so the parameter never bound and
Postgres saw a stray :content::jsonb token. Fixed by switching to CAST(:content AS JSONB) everywhere.

Tested end-to-end against the live container across STUDENT/INSTRUCTOR/ADMIN roles: role gating on evrder conflict handling, 404s for missing levels/materials, the publish/unpublish visibility split(verified public vs. staff vs. student views), JSONB content round-tripping correctly as a Python dict, and delete/re-delete behavior. All test data cleaned up afterward.

