Committed as 06e8ff8. Summary:

Staff management (app/api/testing.py): CRUD for tests (under a material), questions (under a test), a — all gated to INSTRUCTOR/ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN. Unpublished tests are invisible to students, samepattern as materials.

Student attempt flow:
- POST /tests/{id}/attempts — starts a timed attempt; blocks a second concurrent in-progress attempt (403), returns questions+options with correct answers stripped out.
- POST /attempts/{id}/submit — scores each question by exact-set match (so multi-select requires selecting all and only the correct options), computes score/pass against passing_score, rejects unknown question/option IDs (400), and
  enforces the time limit server-side.
- GET /attempts/{id} — owner or staff only; shows per-question breakdown once submitted.
- GET /tests/{id}/attempts/me — a student's own attempt history.

Two real bugs found and fixed while testing:
1. :content::jsonb-style casts in raw SQL silently failed — SQLAlchemy's text() treats :: as an escaped literal colon, so the parameter never bound. Fixed with CAST(:x AS JSONB) (same class of bug as the curriculum-management fix
   earlier, now applied to question_text/option_text).
2. In submit_attempt, marking an attempt TIME_EXPIRED and then raising HTTPException(410) in the same with engine.begin() block caused the status update to be rolled back along with the exception — the attempt stayed stuck as
   IN_PROGRESS in the DB. Fixed by committing the expiry update in its own transaction before raising

Tested end-to-end: full CRUD permission checks, a two-question test (single-choice + multi-select) scss two attempts, max_attempts cutoff, real time-expiry with a 1-second test, re-submit/double-submitrejection, and cross-student access denial (403 view / 404 submit). All test data cleaned up afterward.

