Committed as 8067966. Summary:
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         p/services/notification_service.py — send_notification(conn, ...) generalizes the send-and-log pattMTP service, logs SENT/FAILED + timestamp/error to the notifications table.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         factored to use it:
- certificate_service.py — dropped its duplicated send+log code in favor of the shared helper (verified no regression).                                                                                                                  auth.py — the email-verification send (previously fire-and-forget with no DB record) now logs throuation emails have the same audit trail as certificate emails.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         w:
- POST /auth/resend-verification — CAPTCHA-protected, returns the same generic message whether or not the account exists (avoids email enumeration), only actually sends if the account exists and isn't already verified. This closes a real gap — there was previously no recovery path if the first verification email was lost.
- GET /notifications/me — a student's own notification history.
- GET /notifications — ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN only, all notifications, limit param (capped at 500).

Tested end-to-end: register logs one EMAIL_VERIFICATION notification, resend-verification logs a secoresponse for both a real and a nonexistent account, verifying via the resent token works,/notifications/me shows both entries, STUDENT is blocked from the staff-only list (403), unauthenticated requests are rejected (401), ADMIN can see notifications across all students, and a full certificate-issuance run confirmed the refactor didn't break anything. All test data cleaned up afterward.

