Committed as 9f5aac1. The full stack is running at http://localhost:3000. Summary:

Foundation: Tailwind CSS, a JWT-based AuthProvider (localStorage), a RequireRole route guard, a share primitives (Button, Card, Input, Badge, etc.).

Public/auth: landing page (levels list), registration with a real Turnstile widget, login, email veri flow).

Student: dashboard with certificate/level overview, level→material→test browsing (respects publish stng flow (countdown, single/multi-choice, auto-submit on expiry), results, certificates, notifications.

Instructor/Admin: nested curriculum management (levels → materials → tests → questions → options, eaclete), user management (role changes for SUPER_ADMIN, activate/deactivate for ADMIN+), and anall-notifications view.

Two real issues found and fixed along the way:
1. Missing GET /questions/{id}/options — the option-editing UI had no way to display existing optionsded that staff-only endpoint to the backend.
2. NEXT_PUBLIC_* env vars were only set as container runtime env in docker-compose.yml, but Next.js inlines them at build time — they were silently never taking effect. Fixed by passing them as Docker build args.
3. Caught a stale-closure bug in the test-timer's auto-submit (it would've submitted empty answers on using a ref to track live answer state.

Testing performed: docker compose build succeeds for both services, every route returns 200, the Tailpiled utility classes, build-time env vars are confirmed baked into the JS bundle, and I cross-checked every frontend API call against the actual backend Pydantic schemas.

Not verified: actual browser interaction — this environment has no Node.js locally and no browser/screenshot tooling, only Docker and curl, so I could not click through forms, watch the Turnstile widget render, or see the countdown
timer in action. Worth a manual pass in a real browser before you consider this done.

